# Class: <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000299> (Butcher-Kuntzmann method)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000299> "2011-05-10"^^xsd:date)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000299> "AZ"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000299> "Butcher-Kuntzmann method"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "F. Ceschin, J. Kuntzmann, Problèmes différentiels de conditions initiales. Paris 1963. Dunod."@fr) rdfs:seeAlso <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000299> "http://identifiers.org/doi/10.1002/zamm.19660460519"^^xsd:anyURI)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Butcher, J. C. (1964) Implicit Runge-Kutta processes. Math. Comput. 18, 50-64."@en) rdfs:seeAlso <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000299> "urn:issn:1088-6842(e)"^^xsd:anyURI)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "EXACT"@en) <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000299> "Gauss method"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000299> "From a theoretical point of view, the Butcher-Kuntzmann Runge-Kutta methods belong to the best step-by-step methods for nonstiff problems. These methods integrate first-order initial-value problems by means of formulas based on Gauss-Legendre quadrature, and combine excellent stability features with the property of superconvergence at the step points."@en)
SubClassOf(<http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000299> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000064>)
SubClassOf(<http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000299> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000245> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000103>))
