# Class: <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000418> (N-way partial least squares regression method)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000418> "2012-01-18"^^xsd:date)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000418> "AZ"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000418> "Requested by Kristin Tøndel on Thursday, October 13, 2011 11:33:06 AM."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000418> "N-way partial least squares regression method"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Bro R (1996) Multiway calibration. Multilinear PLS. J. Chemometrics 10: 47-6."@en) rdfs:seeAlso <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000418> "http://identifiers.org/doi/10.1002/(SICI)1099-128X(199601)10:1<47::AID-CEM400>3.0.CO;2-C"^^xsd:anyURI)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "N-way toolbox website"@en) rdfs:seeAlso <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000418> "http://www.models.life.ku.dk/nwaytoolbox"^^xsd:anyURI)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "EXACT"@en) <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000418> "N-PLS"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "EXACT"@en) <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000418> "N-way PLSR"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "EXACT"@en) <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000418> "N-way partial least squares method"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000418> "Multivariate regression method that can be used on N-way data. Based on Partial Least Squares Regression (PLSR) [http://identifiers.org/biomodels.kisao/KISAO_0000416], which is a regression method based on estimated latent variables. PLSR is related to Principal Component Analysis (PCA) and Principal Component Regression (PCR)."@en)
SubClassOf(<http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000418> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000423>)
