# Class: <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000598> (hybrid Gibson - Milstein method)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000598> "2021-01-13"^^xsd:date)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000598> "JRK"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000598> "MLB"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "VCell"@en) <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#isImplementedIn> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000598> "http://identifiers.org/biosimulators/vcell"^^xsd:anyURI)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000598> "hybrid Gibson - Milstein method"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "H.Salis, V. Sotiropoulos and Y. Kaznessis,'Multiscale Hy3S: Hybrid stochastic simulation for supercomputers', BMC Bioinformatics 7:93 (2006)."@en) rdfs:seeAlso <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000598> "http://identifiers.org/doi/10.1186/1471-2105-7-93"^^xsd:anyURI)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000598> "A hybrid stochastic method partitions the system into subsets of fast and slow reactions and approximates the fast reactions as a continuous Markov process, using a chemical Langevin equation, and accurately describes the slow dynamics using the Gibson algorithm. Fixed time step Milstein is used for approximate numerical solution of CLE."@en)
SubClassOf(<http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000598> <http://www.biomodels.net/kisao/KISAO#KISAO_0000352>)
